# The annotations of tape block 1, the BASIC loader "ATV" at PROG $5CCB-$5CF6 (44 bytes): the source of
# src/tape/basic.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/tape/basic.json). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
# Witness: c1 (work/stage1/rec/c1): the ROM loaded it and ran it; the loader at $FFDC ran from frame 1017.

@module basic ; The BASIC loader: CLEAR, LOAD ""CODE, RANDOMIZE USR into the machine-code loader
@about Three lines, as LIST shows them: 10 CLEAR 25400, 20 LOAD ""CODE, 30 RANDOMIZE USR 65500. CLEAR puts RAMTOP at $6338 (25400), the first byte of the game; LOAD ""CODE reads tape blocks 2 and 3, the loader, to $FFDC; RANDOMIZE USR 65500 enters it. Every number is written as the ROM writes it: its digits, then $0E and the five-byte form (a small integer: 0, 0, the value low byte first, 0). No machine code reads these bytes; the ROM's interpreter does.

$5CCB b BasicLine10 ; Line 10: CLEAR 25400
> The line number high byte first (0, 10), the length low byte first (13), the token CLEAR ($FD), the digits "25400", $0E and the number 25400 ($6338) in the ROM's small-integer form, $0D. Read by the ROM's interpreter in c1.
$5CDC b BasicLine20 ; Line 20: LOAD ""CODE
> Line 20 (0, 20), length 5: LOAD ($EF), two quotes (the empty name), CODE ($AF), $0D. The ROM loads the next CODE block to the address its header gives, $FFDC (tape blocks 2 and 3).
$5CE5 b BasicLine30 ; Line 30: RANDOMIZE USR 65500
> Line 30 (0, 30), length 14: RANDOMIZE ($F9), USR ($C0), "65500", $0E and 65500 ($FFDC) in the small-integer form, $0D. USR calls the loader at $FFDC (c1, frame 1017).
